{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (cobbler orchestrator) issued stitch task #5646 to implement four specific requirements for `cmd/ts` (timestamp stdin lines utility):\n   - **R1.5**: Pass through partial lines (lines not terminated by newline at EOF) with a timestamp prefix\n   - **R1.6**: Exit code must be 0 after stdin EOF. Must not exit non-zero due to SIGPIPE when stdout is closed by downstream consumer\n   - **R2.1**: Accept an optional positional argument specifying a custom strftime format string (e.g., `ts '%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'`)\n   - **R2.2**: Support all standard strftime(3) conversion specifications available on the target platform\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/ts/main.go` (modify) and `cmd/ts/ts_test.go` (modify/create - it doesn't exist yet).\n   \n   Acceptance criteria: compilation without errors, all tests pass including new ones, go vet clean, each requirement has at least one differential test case.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Differential testing**: Tests compare Go binary output against moreutils `ts` reference binary (no g-prefix)\n   - **strftime format conversion**: Go uses time.Format with layout strings, not strftime. Need to convert strftime specifiers (like `%Y`, `%m`, `%d`, `%H`, `%M`, `%S`) to Go equivalents\n   - **Partial line handling**: bufio.Scanner drops the last line if no trailing newline - need bufio.Reader approach instead\n   - **SIGPIPE handling**: sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() already called; ensures clean exit when downstream closes pipe\n   - **testutils.TimestampNormalizer**: Must be used in DiffTest.Normalize slice to replace wall-clock timestamps with fixed placeholder\n   - **testutils.RunDiffTests**: Standard differential testing function\n   - **testutils.BuildBinary**: Builds the cmd/ binary for testing\n   - **Function size limit**: 40 lines hard limit (E8)\n   - **File size limit**: 500 lines (E9)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd004-ts.yaml**\n     - Full SRD for ts utility with all requirements R1-R10\n     - R1.5: \"Must pass through partial lines (lines not terminated by a newline at EOF) with a timestamp prefix.\"\n     - R1.6: \"Exit code must be 0 after stdin is closed with EOF. Must not exit non-zero due to SIGPIPE when stdout is closed by a downstream consumer.\"\n     - R2.1: \"Must accept an optional positional argument specifying a custom strftime format string\"\n     - R2.2: \"Must support all standard strftime(3) conversion specifications available on the target platform.\"\n     - Non-goals include: no --help/--version flags, no file reading, no localized date parsing\n   \n   - **cmd/ts/main.go** (existing, needs modification)\n     - Current implementation only covers R1.1-R1.4\n     - Full current content:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     // Implements srd004-ts R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4.\n     package main\n     \n     import (\n         \"bufio\"\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"time\"\n     \n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         os.Exit(run())\n     }\n     \n     func run() int {\n         scanner := bufio.NewScanner(os.Stdin)\n         for scanner.Scan() {\n             line := scanner.Text()\n             ts := time.Now().Format(\"Jan 02 15:04:05\")\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"%s %s\\n\", ts, line)\n         }\n         return 0\n     }\n     ```\n     - Problems: Uses bufio.Scanner (drops partial last lines), hardcodes format, no argument parsing\n   \n   - **cmd/ts/ts_test.go** - Does NOT exist yet, needs to be created\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - cmd/ts/ts_test.go returned \"File does not exist\" when Read was attempted. This means the test file must be created from scratch, not modified.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   Key implementation challenges identified but not yet addressed:\n   - **Partial lines (R1.5)**: bufio.Scanner silently drops lines without trailing newline. Need to switch to bufio.Reader with ReadString('\\n') or similar approach that returns partial lines at EOF.\n   - **strftime conversion (R2.1, R2.2)**: Go has no native strftime. Must implement a strftime-to-Go-format converter or a direct strftime formatter. Common mappings: `%Y`→`2006`, `%m`→`01`, `%d`→`02`, `%H`→`15`, `%M`→`04`, `%S`→`05`, `%b`→`Jan`, `%T`→`15:04:05`, etc.\n   - **Argument parsing**: Need to parse os.Args to detect flags vs positional format string argument. Current code has no flag parsing at all.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - One massive stitch task message containing: role definition, repository file listing, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement states), execution constitution, go style constitution, task description with requirements R1.5/R1.6/R2.1/R2.2, design decisions, acceptance criteria, shared protocols, and package contracts.\n   - \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a summary of conversation state.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Implement R1.5 (partial line handling) in cmd/ts/main.go\n   - Implement R1.6 (proper exit code handling) in cmd/ts/main.go \n   - Implement R2.1 (custom format string positional argument) in cmd/ts/main.go\n   - Implement R2.2 (strftime conversion support) in cmd/ts/main.go\n   - Create cmd/ts/ts_test.go with differential tests for all four requirements\n   - Verify: `go build ./cmd/ts/` compiles, `go test ./cmd/ts/... -count=1` passes, `go vet ./cmd/ts/` is clean\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just completed reading the three required files (SRD, existing main.go, and attempted to read nonexistent test file) and was about to begin the implementation phase. No code has been written yet. The plan phase was in progress - I had identified what needs to change:\n   \n   For **cmd/ts/main.go**:\n   - Replace `bufio.Scanner` with `bufio.Reader` to handle partial lines (R1.5)\n   - Add argument parsing for optional format string (R2.1)\n   - Implement strftime-to-Go-time-format conversion (R2.2)\n   - Update package comment to include R1.5, R1.6, R2.1, R2.2\n   - SIGPIPE already handled (R1.6 partially done)\n   \n   For **cmd/ts/ts_test.go** (create new):\n   - Use differential testing pattern with testutils.BuildBinary and exec.LookPath(\"ts\")\n   - Use testutils.TimestampNormalizer in DiffTest.Normalize\n   - Add test cases for: partial lines, custom format strings, strftime specifiers, clean EOF exit\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write the implementation for cmd/ts/main.go adding R1.5, R1.6, R2.1, R2.2 support, then create cmd/ts/ts_test.go with differential tests. The task description states: \"Implement srd004-ts R1.5 per the SRD acceptance criteria\", \"Implement srd004-ts R1.6 per the SRD acceptance criteria\", \"Implement srd004-ts R2.1 per the SRD acceptance criteria\", \"Implement srd004-ts R2.2 per the SRD acceptance criteria\". Design decision D1 says: \"Extend the existing cmd/ts implementation -- do not rewrite or restructure existing code from R1.1-R1.4\". The go_style_constitution says: \"Write all source files before running any build or test commands.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5646/6cf36243-788b-4262-aaeb-9b394f2db82f.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do 