{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JQ2FBNuRCxoHEZWsfZSvyM","type":"tool_result","content":"  - id: srd004-ts\n    title: \"cmd/ts: Timestamp Stdin Lines\"\n    summary: Prepend strftime timestamps to each stdin line with incremental, elapsed, monotonic, and relative modes.\n    path: docs/specs/software-requirements/srd004-ts.yaml\n  - id: srd005-wc\n    title: \"cmd/wc: Count Lines, Words, and Bytes\"\n    summary: Count lines, words, bytes, characters, and max line length from files or stdin.\n    path: docs/specs/software-requirements/srd005-wc.yaml\n  - id: srd006-cat\n    title: \"cmd/cat: Concatenate and Display Files\"\n    summary: Concatenate files to stdout with line numbering, blank squeezing, and non-printing display.\n    path: docs/specs/software-requirements/srd006-cat.yaml\n  - id: srd007-sponge\n    title: \"cmd/sponge: Soak Stdin and Write to File\"\n    summary: Buffer all stdin before opening the output file, enabling safe in-place pipeline rewrites.\n    path: docs/specs/software-requirements/srd007-sponge.yaml\n  - id: srd008-ls\n    title: \"cmd/ls: Core File Listing\"\n    summary: List directory contents with all output formats, sorting, filtering, metadata display, color, classification, and recursive listing.\n    path: docs/specs/software-requirements/srd008-ls.yaml\n  - id: srd009-du\n    title: \"cmd/du: Recursive Directory Disk Usage\"\n    summary: Report disk usage with recursive traversal, hard-link deduplication, and human-readable output.\n    path: docs/specs/software-requirements/srd009-du.yaml\n  - id: srd059-version\n    title: \"cmd/version: Version Identity Binary\"\n    summary: A cmd/version binary that prints the repository's last known version tag, with ldflags injection and an exported version variable.\n    path: docs/specs/software-requirements/srd059-version.yaml\n  - id: srd012-yes\n    title: \"cmd/yes: Repeatedly Output a String\"\n    summary: Output a string repeatedly until killed, with buffered writes for throughput.\n    path: docs/specs/software-requirements/srd012-yes.yaml\n  - id: srd013-true\n    title: \"cmd/true: Exit Successfully\"\n    summary: Exit with status 0, ignoring all arguments.\n    path: docs/specs/software-requirements/srd013-true.yaml\n  - id: srd014-false\n    title: \"cmd/false: Exit Unsuccessfully\"\n    summary: Exit with status 1, ignoring all arguments.\n    path: docs/specs/software-requirements/srd014-false.yaml\n  - id: srd015-basename\n    title: \"cmd/basename: Strip Directory and Suffix from Filenames\"\n    summary: Strip directory prefix and optional suffix from file paths with multi-argument and NUL-delimited modes.\n    path: docs/specs/software-requirements/srd015-basename.yaml\n  - id: srd016-dirname\n    title: \"cmd/dirname: Strip Last Component from File Paths\"\n    summary: Extract directory component from file paths with NUL-delimited output mode.\n    path: docs/specs/software-requirements/srd016-dirname.yaml\n  - id: srd017-tee\n    title: \"cmd/tee: Read Stdin and Write to Stdout and Files\"\n    summary: Copy stdin to stdout and one or more files with append mode and SIGINT suppression.\n    path: docs/specs/software-requirements/srd017-tee.yaml\n  - id: srd018-head\n    title: \"cmd/head: Print the First Lines or Bytes of Files\"\n--\n    srd: srd004-ts\n    why_required: ts exercises timestamp prepending with multiple time modes and strftime formatting.\n    coverage: Full — all srd004-ts requirement groups (R1-R8) are traced from the test suite.\n\n  - use_case: rel02.0-uc001-true\n    srd: srd013-true\n    why_required: true is the simplest possible utility, validating the build pipeline for trivial binaries.\n    coverage: Full — all srd013-true requirement groups (R1-R4) are traced from the test suite.\n  - use_case: rel02.0-uc002-false\n    srd: srd014-false\n    why_required: false validates non-zero exit code handling in the differential testing harness.\n    coverage: Full