{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xho3hJ6oofUunXpZoDTbY3","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me create a comprehensive summary of my findings:\n\n## Summary of Patterns and Constraints for cmd/ts Implementation\n\nBased on my thorough search of the go-unix-utils codebase, here are the key patterns and constraints you'll need for implementing cmd/ts:\n\n### 1. **testutils Package Structure** (`pkg/testutils/`)\n\n**TimestampNormalizer:**\n- Located at `/pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (lines 57-72)\n- Type: `NormalizeFunc` (function type defined as `func([]byte) []byte`)\n- Purpose: Replaces common strftime timestamp patterns with fixed placeholder `<TIMESTAMP>`\n- Pattern matches (from tsPatterns regex):\n  - Syslog format: `[A-Z][a-z]{2}\\s+\\d{1,2}\\s+\\d{2}:\\d{2}:\\d{2}` (e.g., \"May 13 14:30:00\")\n  - ISO format: `\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}\\s+\\d{2}:\\d{2}:\\d{2}` (e.g., \"2026-05-13 14:30:00\")\n  - Time-only format: `\\d{2}:\\d{2}:\\d{2}` (e.g., \"14:30:00\")\n\n**DiffTest Struct Fields:**\n- `Name` (string): Test case identifier used with `t.Run()`\n- `Args` ([]string): Command-line arguments passed to both binaries\n- `Stdin` ([]byte): Input data; nil means EOF immediately, empty []byte{} means open stdin\n- `Env` ([]string): Environment variable KEY=VALUE pairs merged into inherited environment\n- `WorkDir` (string): Working directory; empty string defaults to `t.TempDir()`\n- `ExitCode` (int): Expected exit code (defaults to 0)\n- `Normalize` ([]NormalizeFunc): Slice of normalization functions applied to stdout/stderr before comparison\n- `ExpectedFiles` (map[string][]byte): Expected file contents to verify after test execution\n\n**RunDiffTests Function:**\n- Signature: `RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)`\n- Runs each DiffTest as a named subtest with `t.Run()`\n- Executes both goBinary and refBinary with identical inputs\n- Compares outputs (stdout, stderr, exit code) after applying normalizers\n\n**BuildBinary Function:**\n- Signature: `BuildBinary(t *testing.T, dir string) string`\n- Compiles Go package at `dir` using `go build`\n- Returns path to compiled binary\n- Fatal on compilation failure\n- Binary placed in temporary directory cleaned up on test completion\n- Package name resolved from directory base name\n\n**ComposeNormalizers Function:**\n- Signature: `ComposeNormalizers(fns ...NormalizeFunc) NormalizeFunc`\n- Combines multiple normalizers to apply in sequence\n- Useful for chaining TimestampNormalizer with other custom normalizers\n\n### 2. **strftime/Time Format Conversion**\n\n**Existing strftime Implementation:**\n- Found in `cmd/date/main.go` - full strftime implementation with all conversion specs\n- Key pattern: `formatTime()` function (lines 124-153) parses format strings and applies specs\n- Supports all standard strftime specs (%Y, %m, %d, %H, %M, %S, %a, %A, %b, %B, %Z, %z, etc.)\n- Supports padding modifiers: `-` (no pad), `_` (space pad), `0` (zero pad)\n- `numSpec()` and `textSpec()` functions separated for numerical vs text specs\n\n**ts-Specific Subsecond Extensions (from srd004-ts):**\n- `%.S`: Seconds with microsecond suffix (e.g., \"32.001234\")\n- `%.s`: Unix epoch with microsecond suffix (e.g., \"1708358732.001234\")\n- `%.T`: HH:MM:SS with microsecond suffix (e.g., \"14:05:32.001234\")\n- Must use `time.Now()` sub-nanosecond precision formatted to 6 decimal places\n- Must be atomic (single time sample per line)\n\n**Default Format:**\n- Default: `\"%b %d %H:%M:%S\"` (e.g., \"Feb 19 14:05:32\")\n- In `-i` and `-s` modes: `\"%H:%M:%S\"` with `TZ=GMT`\n\n### 3. **Differential Test Patterns** (from existing test files)\n\n**From cmd/cat/cat_test.go:**\n- Calls `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` to build the binary\n- Uses `exec.LookPath()` to find reference binary, skips test if not found\n- Creates test cases with `[]testutils.DiffTest{}`\n- Calls `testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)`\n- Uses SIGPIPE test pattern with `exec.CommandContext()` and timeout\n\n**From cmd/tee/tee_test.go:**\n- Demonstrates helper functions for test setup (e.g., `runFileTest()`, `runMultiFileTest()`)\n- Shows manual exec.Command usage for non-DiffTest scenarios\n- Verifies file creation and content modification\n- Tests error handling and exit codes\n- Uses t.TempDir() for test isolation\n\n**From cmd/md5sum/md5sum_test.go:**\n- Shows use of NormalizeFunc (discardStderr): `testutils.NormalizeFunc(func([]byte) []byte { return nil })`\n- Demonstrates composition patterns with multiple test variations\n- Shows how to verify file operations alongside stdout/stderr\n- Shows multi-file test scenarios\n\n### 4. **Go Style Constitution Constraints** (docs/constitutions/go-style.yaml)\n\n**Function Size:**\n- No function should exceed **200 lines** without a strong reason (line 371)\n- If a function grows beyond 200 lines, find a seam and split it\n\n**File Organization:**\n- Within a file: constants/types first, then constructors (NewXxx), then exported methods/functions, then unexported helpers, main() last\n- Name files by concern, not by kind (no helpers.go, types.go, utils.go)\n- Tests go in `<file>_test.go` alongside the file they test\n\n**Function Parameters:**\n- If a function takes more than 3 parameters, group related parameters into a config struct (line 137)\n- For cmd/ts, use a config struct for flags\n\n**Error Handling:**\n- Handle errors at the point they occur with guard clauses\n- Wrap errors with fmt.Errorf(\"doing X: %w\", err)\n- Never silently discard errors except for best-effort cleanup (with comment)\n\n**Testing Requirements:**\n- Every exported function and meaningful branch deserves a test\n- Use table-driven parameterized tests\n- Call `t.Parallel()` as first line in every test safe to run concurrently\n- Call `t.Helper()` as first line of every test helper function\n\n**No boolean parameters:**\n- Do not use boolean flags to toggle behavior that should be a Strategy or Decorator pattern\n\n### 5. **Testing Constitution** (docs/constitutions/testing.yaml)\n\n**Test Naming (NOT required for cmd/ts based on existing code):**\n- Pattern: `Test{Suite}_UC{NNN}_DescriptiveName`\n- However, existing cmd tests (cat, tee, md5sum) use simpler names like `TestDiff`, `TestDiffSIGPIPE`\n\n**Test Organization:**\n- Tests in `<cmd>_test.go` alongside implementation\n- One test file per command\n\n### 6. **Existing ts Implementation** (`cmd/ts/main.go`)\n\nCurrently implements basic R1 (default behavior):\n```go\nfunc main() {\n    sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n    os.Exit(run())\n}\n\nfunc run() int {\n    scanner := bufio.NewScanner(os.Stdin)\n    for scanner.Scan() {\n        line := scanner.Text()\n        ts := time.Now().Format(\"Jan 02 15:04:05\")\n        fmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"%s %s\\n\", ts, line)\n    }\n    return 0\n}\n```\n\n**Missing from current implementation:**\n- Custom format string support (R2)\n- Incremental mode `-i` (R3)\n- Elapsed-since-start mode `-s` (R4)\n- Monotonic clock mode `-m` (R5)\n- Relative-time parsing and age output `-r` (R6)\n- Proper error handling and exit codes (R7)\n- TZ environment handling (R8)\n- Tests with DiffTest harness (R9)\n\n### 7. **Signal Handling Pattern**\n\nAll utilities import and use:\n```go\nimport \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n```\n\nIn main():\n```go\nsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\nos.Exit(run())\n```\n\nThis pattern is used across cat, date, tee, md5sum, and other utilities.\n\n### 8. **Key Implementation Patterns to Follow**\n\n1. **All files before compilation**: Write all source files (main.go, types, helpers) before running `go build` or `go test` - avoids incremental loops\n2. **Config struct**: For flag parsing, use a config struct with fields for each option\n3. **Error wrapping**: Use `fmt.Errorf(\"context: %w\", err)` for meaningful error messages\n4. **Output flushing**: R1.3 requires flushing stdout after each line - use `os.Stdout.WriteString()` or `fmt.Fprintf()` which auto-flushes, or explicit flush with `os.Stdout.Sync()`\n5. **Exit codes**: Return 0 for success, 1 for errors\n6. **Environment**: For TZ handling, use `os.Setenv()` for internal test-safe approaches, or construct time values that respect user's TZ\n7. **Testing**: Use TestDiff with TimestampNormalizer for wall-clock timestamps, separate tests for each mode (-i, -s, -m, -r)\n\n### 9. **Key Files to Reference**\n\n- `/pkg/testutils/difftest.go` - Full testutils API and TimestampNormalizer\n- `/cmd/date/main.go` - Complete strftime implementation pattern\n- `/cmd/cat/cat_test.go` - Example DiffTest usage pattern\n- `/cmd/tee/tee_test.go` - Complex test helper patterns\n- `/cmd/md5sum/md5sum_test.go` - NormalizeFunc usage examples\n- `/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd004-ts.yaml` - Full ts specification with all requirements"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6cf36243-788b-4262-aaeb-9b394f2db82f","uuid":"9b60a5c8-bdb1-4546-a6d6-cd489c148fca","timestamp":"2026-05-29T16:00:55.110Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand patterns in this Go codebase for implementing cmd/ts. Please find:\n\n1. The testutils package - specifically how TimestampNormalizer is defined, how DiffTest struct looks (fields), how RunDiffTests and BuildBinary work. Read pkg/testutils/ files.\n\n2. Any existing strftime conversion code in the codebase - search for \"strftime\" in all Go files. Also look for any Go time format conversion utilities.\n\n3. Look at a few example test files in cmd/ directories to see the differential testing pattern (e.g., cmd/cat/cat_test.go or any other that exists). I need to see how tests are structured with DiffTest, Normalize, etc.\n\n4. Check if there's a pkg/strftime or similar package.\n\n5. Read the go style constitution at docs/constitutions/ - specifically look for function size limits, file size limits, and any other constraints.\n\nSearch breadth: very thorough